KigEyes IMX675 core driver licensing
=================================

The following core-release files are distributed under the GNU General
Public License version 2 only (GPL-2.0-only). See COPYING for the full text:

  imx675_kigeyes.c
  imx675_regs.h
  Makefile
  install.sh
  overlays/kigeyes-imx675-overlay.dts
  overlays/kigeyes-imx675-dual-overlay.dts
  overlays/kigeyes-imx675-dual-sync-overlay.dts
  overlays/kigeyes-imx675-mainboard-sync-overlay.dts
  systemd/kigeyes-imx675-mainboard.conf
  README.md

For these files, this explicit component license takes precedence over the
parent repository's default software license. The kernel source headers'
GPL-2.0 identifier means version 2 only, consistent with Linux conventions.

The sensor initialization values in imx675_regs.h were adapted from the
FRAMOS IMX675 driver, copyright (c) 2024 Framos, revision
4e772feec7f21e5ca3d485142c7df03a95c75f3c of:
https://github.com/framosimaging/framos-jetson-drivers
The upstream source declares GPL-2.0. Its attribution is retained in the
register header. Explicit file licenses take precedence over the parent
repository's general software-license notice.

Separate libcamera integration and application components are not covered
by this core-export license. Their existing licenses are unchanged; preserve
their own notices if distributed. Sony documents and vendor source checkouts
are not included in the core export.
